WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm always so flattered
and honored

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
when people who are currently
doing a Broadway show

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.404 line:92%
come to this show because

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.905 size:84% position:42%
you really only have
the one day off a week,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.274
and yet, you have chosen
to spend your Monday here.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think to be
on Broadway,

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:11.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
you just have to give up
having any days off.

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Just forget it.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.547 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Has it been daunting?

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because obviously you've done
film and television.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not only is the work
so different,

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the schedule
is so different.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that being, you know,
the lead of a Broadway play

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
is hands down the hardest job
in show business.

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I believe it.
-But incredibly satisfying.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are -- the show,
you play a socialite in D.C.,

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.735
this is a very topical show,
who is trying to get her husband

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.772
a job as a judge in the Trump
administration via blackmail.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Via blackmail.
-Yeah.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
-Of course. Why not?

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.278
-What else are you going to use?
-Guys, there's maybe

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:47.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
some shady stuff happening
in D.C.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The egalitarian system,
we're done with it.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're just pure nepotism,
pure blackmail.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So -- but you and I have
something similar,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.989 line:92%
which is, we obviously, are both

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
talking about the world
in our jobs.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:00:59.926 line:92%
So it's not really escapism.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you finding --
is it cathartic to talk about

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump or is it --
do you find it overwhelming?

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:09.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, huh, I would say
overwhelming as an American.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And as a patriot.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But as an artist,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:18.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a lot of fun.
But, no, it's --

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.214
I was involved with a play
when it was written about

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:24.284
a Washington couple and sort of
the bedroom mischief,

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's very naughty,
liberated woman that I play,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:30.957
but then Trump was elected while
we were developing the play,

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:35.395
so naturally, the world changed
and it became this --

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's kind of like one person
described it as like

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.934 size:81% position:41%
a rock concert almost,
because the audience

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:46.039
is getting such a sort of,
like, a relief of laughter

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:49.375
and sort of bitter irony
and they kind of let loose.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.444
-You do have something that's --
-Like they do here.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
Something that's very risky,

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.182 size:81% position:41% line:92%
though, because plays,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:59.719
we can change based on the news
every day what we write.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:00.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-You guys have a play that's

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.156
written, John Kelly is mentioned
a lot in the show.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
-14 times.
-14 times.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:08.428
-Oh, yeah. I just had a count
done just a couple weeks ago.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
-But 14 times a day,

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.765
I feel as though we hear rumors
that he's about to be fired.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's true.
-What would happen --

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:16.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or possibly say
enough is enough.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:17.370 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Or leave. Exactly.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.273
We should give him the power
to make his own choices, yeah.

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.241 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I mean, definitely.

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:25.612
-Have you guys discussed what
would happen if that changed?

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:29.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There was some e-mails went
around the last few weeks

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:32.619
where I was kind of like,
contingency plan, please,

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the play
will have to pivot.

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, absolutely.
-I wrote a lengthy play

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
about Anthony Scaramucci.
-And it just didn't work out.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Actually, Beau Willimon

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.730
said to me when we were in --
before rehearsal, he was like,

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.833
"I was really looking forward
to making you say Scaramucci,

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.767 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Scaramucci, Scaramucci."

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Scaramucci
is far more fun to say.

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:52.272 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Just turned into Kelly.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.806 line:92%
-So, I wanted to ask about this,

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:56.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
you grew up -- you had
a very interesting upbringing.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:03:00.647
And now I have a 2-year-old
and we spend a lot of time,

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
my wife and I, talking about
the things you talk about

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:05.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of your child,
intelligent conversations.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your father
was a Buddhist scholar.

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:10.056 size:78% position:39%
So did you -- was the
conversation around

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
your dinner table growing up,
was it incredibly, like,

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just enlightened,
but intellectually superior

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the point --
-It was usually, like,

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
eat your dinner!
[ Laughs ]

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That does not seem in line
with Buddhists.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Have your vegetables!
-Yeah.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:25.271 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-No, but well, you know,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:29.642
growing up in an academic
environment can be challenging.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:33.713
It's good for you to be prepared
for the hard-hitting brains

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.814 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of Hollywood.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But, You Know --

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-All that hard work.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.954 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:45.058 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But, no, it was good.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good debate skills.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.928
-I think my dad had been, like,
captain of the debate team

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:51.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he went to school.
-I think that's very helpful.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.267
I think arguing is the one skill
that's helpful --

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Follow the ball.
-Yeah,

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:59.706
it's helpful in all fields.
-Thinking in general, actually.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:01.441
-Thinking in general is helpful,
yeah.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:04.811 size:88% position:44%
Now, did you have, like,
sort of escapism things

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you liked as a kid?
-I went to Hollywood.

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:09.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
You got to meet --

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.316 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I escaped all the way.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got to meet
another scholar backstage.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:14.687
And this is a really exciting --
-Yes, a woman whom I love.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A woman you love.
There's Dr. Ruth.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:20.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Dr. Ruth. Best time ever.
Not our first meeting, though.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I got to be honest,
I had thought you were taller

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.098 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
than her.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:25.865 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you know, she grew.
She grew.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, she's a very --
how was that?

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.537 size:88% position:44%
I mean, that must be one
of the fun things to do

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your Broadway show, is
the people who come backstage.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:36.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, really great
seeing great people

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.645
including, like, distant family,
relatives, like,

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:41.981
that you wouldn't have met that,
like, come and see your play.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, they're just lying
to get backstage.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:46.753
-Hi, I'm your cousin.
No, it's been on a family level

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:47.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
actually,
it's been really fun.

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:49.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-Yeah, I've gotten to meet

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:53.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
some relatives from down South
that I never grew up with.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:55.528 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But Dr. Ruth is a gem.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:59.365
My character is so sexually
promiscuous and naughty.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:02.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
She really appreciated her.
-Oh, that's good.

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:03.970 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Did she have any notes

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
or did it all ring true
to Dr. Ruth?

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.739
-She thought it was --
I was doing well with it.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:10.176
-That's great. Well, that's
the highest praise you can get.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.010 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-That really was good.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.046 size:78% position:39%
-Hey, congratulations
so much on the show.

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-I also want to say you had

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
a wonderful piece
in "The New York Times"

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:19.852 size:81% position:41%
about your experiences
with Harvey Weinstein

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:20.720 line:92%
on the set of "Kill Bill."

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
I, you know, I think it's
been so wonderful how people

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:25.425
are speaking out about
their experiences in this moment

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're having right now.
And I just wanted to thank you

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.829
for doing that, as well.
-Well, you got to be a citizen.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't leave people alone
holding a bag of truth

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
by themselves.
-That's very -- I'm glad --

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:39.172 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:43.743 line:92%
-But there's no one I wish

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:46.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get due process
more than him.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:48.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Well, due process
is a beautiful thing.

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much for
being here. Such a pleasure.

